adjective: Virgin Islander","ordinal":33,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:33","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Ethnic groups","content":"black 76.2%, white 13.1%, Asian 1.1%, other 6.1%, mixed 3.5% (2000 census)","ordinal":34,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:34","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Religions","content":"Baptist 42%, Roman Catholic 34%, Episcopalian 17%, other 7%","ordinal":35,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:35","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Languages","content":"English 74.7%, Spanish or Spanish Creole 16.8%, French or French Creole 6.6%, other 1.9% (2000 census)","ordinal":36,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:36","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"people-and-society","label":"Literacy","content":"definition: age 15 and over can read and write\n\ntotal population: 90-95% est.\n\nmale: NA%\n\nfemale: NA% (2005 est.)","ordinal":37,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:37","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Country name","content":"conventional long form: United States Virgin Islands\n\nconventional short form: Virgin Islands\n\nformer: Danish West Indies\n\nabbreviation: USVI","ordinal":38,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:38","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Dependency status","content":"organized, unincorporated territory of the US with policy relations between the Virgin Islands and the US under the jurisdiction of the Office of Insular Affairs, US Department of the Interior","ordinal":39,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:39","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Government type","content":"NA","ordinal":40,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:40","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Capital","content":"name: Charlotte Amalie\n\ngeographic coordinates: 18 21 N, 64 56 W\n\ntime difference: UTC-4 (1 hour ahead of Washington, DC during Standard Time)","ordinal":41,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:41","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Administrative divisions","content":"none (territory of the US); there are no first-order administrative divisions as defined by the US Government, but there are three islands at the second order; Saint Croix, Saint John, Saint Thomas","ordinal":42,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:42","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Independence","content":"none (territory of the US)","ordinal":43,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:43","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"National holiday","content":"Transfer Day (from Denmark to the US), 27 March (1917)","ordinal":44,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:44","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Constitution","content":"Revised Organic Act of 22 July 1954","ordinal":45,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:45","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legal system","content":"based on US laws","ordinal":46,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:46","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Suffrage","content":"18 years of age; universal; island residents are US citizens but do not vote in US presidential elections","ordinal":47,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:47","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Executive branch","content":"chief of state: President George W. BUSH of the US (since 20 January 2001); Vice President Richard B. CHENEY (since 20 January 2001)\n\nhead of government: Governor John DeJONGH (since 1 January 2007)\n\ncabinet: NA\n\nelections: under the US Constitution, residents of unincorporated territories, such as the Virgin Islands, do not vote in elections for US president and vice president; governor and lieutenant governor elected on the same ticket by popular vote for four-year terms (eligible for a second term); election last held 7 and 21 November 2006 (next to be held November 2010)\n\nelection results: John DeJONGH elected governor; percent of vote - John DeJONGH 57.3%, Kenneth MAPP 42.7%","ordinal":48,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:48","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Legislative branch","content":"unicameral Senate (15 seats; members are elected by popular vote to serve two-year terms)\n\nelections: last held 7 November 2006 (next to be held November 2008)\n\nelection results: percent of vote by party - NA; seats by party - Democratic Party 8, ICM 4, independent 3\n\nnote: the Virgin Islands elects one non-voting representative to the US House of Representatives; election last held 7 November 2006 (next to be held November 2008)","ordinal":49,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:49","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Judicial branch","content":"US District Court of the Virgin Islands (under Third Circuit jurisdiction); Superior Court of the Virgin Islands (judges appointed by the governor for 10-year terms)","ordinal":50,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:50","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political parties and leaders","content":"Democratic Party [Arturo WATLINGTON]; Independent Citizens' Movement or ICM [Usie RICHARDS]; Republican Party [Gary SPRAUVE]","ordinal":51,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:51","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Political pressure groups and leaders","content":"NA","ordinal":52,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:52","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"International organization participation","content":"IOC, UPU","ordinal":53,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:53","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation in the US","content":"none (territory of the US)","ordinal":54,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:54","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Diplomatic representation from the US","content":"none (territory of the US)","ordinal":55,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:55","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"government","label":"Flag description","content":"white, with a modified US coat of arms in the center between the large blue initials V and I; the coat of arms shows a yellow eagle holding an olive branch in one talon and three arrows in the other with a superimposed shield of vertical red and white stripes below a blue panel","ordinal":56,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:56","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"Economy - overview","content":"Tourism is the primary economic activity, accounting for 80% of GDP and employment. The islands hosted 2.6 million visitors in 2005. The manufacturing sector consists of petroleum refining, textiles, electronics, pharmaceuticals, and watch assembly. One of the world's largest petroleum refineries is at Saint Croix. The agricultural sector is small, with most food being imported. International business and financial services are small but growing components of the economy. The islands are vulnerable to substantial damage from storms. The government is working to improve fiscal discipline, to support construction projects in the private sector, to expand tourist facilities, to reduce crime, and to protect the environment.","ordinal":57,"locator":"factbook-2007/geos/vq.html#field:57","country":"VI","edition_year":2007},{"category":"economy","label":"GDP (purchasing power parity)","content":"$1.577 billion (2004 est.)","ordinal":58,"locator":"factbook-2007/g